<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104070" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίτᾰνος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέτανος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a white earth</i>, prob. <i>gypsum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alex.</u>
				21
			</span></i>: also, <i>chalk, lime</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				383b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				389a28
			</span></i>; mixed with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλιξ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.4.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐσβεσμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					2.3
				</span></i>
			; opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ζῶσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					1.393
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκου τὴν ἐκ τῆς τ. διασῴζοντος
				ποιότητα</span> (a cause of insanity) <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.531
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ὕδατι βραχεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18(2).202
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαβὼν τ. θερμὴν φύρασον ὄξει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHolm.</u>
					4.9
				</span></i>
			: meaning indeterm. in <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.124
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. μέλαινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hippiatr.</u>
					80
				</span></i>
			; <i>tetanos, = galbanus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>: also, <i>marble-scrapings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Somn.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. (Perh. from the Thessalian placename <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τίτανος</span>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τιτάνοιό τε λευκὰ κάρηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.735
				</span></i>
			, not conversely as Sch.Il.l.c.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
